 "text": "Hi, how's everything with you? Sloppy shifts usually come from greasy fingers or dirt on the chain. Make sure you' washing your hands before you ride and keep the chain clean and lubed. That's a simple metal ring with a keyhole twist it. Turn it as far as it wants to go, about half a turn. If it starts to tighten against the wheel, stop and put a bit more oil on the rings. It often doesn't. A worn pad needs replacing, which is easy but you need tools. Have you got a spare minute?",
